{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implemented story A (remove inline compact-on-close).\n\nChanges:\n- `src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py` — deleted `_compact_on_close` and its call site; the close tail now ends at scratch cleanup + best-effort push. Left a comment at the removal site recording the measured 13m53s hold, why the 7084 stand-aside probe could not help (the closing process released the lock seconds before its own probe), and where the trigger went.\n- `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_compact_on_close_skip_7084.py` — deleted; every test in it exercised the removed function.\n- `tests/unit/test_transition_close.py` — dropped the two monkeypatches of the removed name (the tests no longer need compaction disabled, which is itself the point).\n- `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_close_does_not_compact_barbet.py` — new, 4 tests.\n- `docs/concurrency.md` — new invariant section I9b 'Compaction runs out of band, never on the close path', plus a correction to I9a (which told operators to avoid closing tickets through a compact-on-close path during a downgrade window — that path no longer exists).\n- `CHANGELOG.md` — Unreleased/Removed entry naming the one user-visible effect: event logs stay unfolded longer, larger on disk, identical in meaning.\n\nRED verified, not assumed: temporarily restoring an inline `compact_cli` call in the close tail fails 2 of the 4 new tests, including the sampler test, which caught the store write lock held while the SNAPSHOT and .retired sources already existed. Restoring the fix makes all 4 pass.\n\nThe sampler test's oracle is a forbidden STATE, not a duration: it samples (lock dir exists?, fold artifacts exist?) every 20ms across the close and asserts the two are never simultaneously true. No timing budget, so nothing for the wall-clock-assert gate to reject and nothing to go flaky under load.\n\nGates so far: 15/15 scripts/check_*.py pass (the three that 'failed' were argument-less invocations of scripts that require flags — re-run correctly, e.g. check_complexity_baseline.py --check reports active=59 new=0 increased=0 stale=0); module-size 0 violations against the 800 cap; make lint and make typecheck clean (518 files); all five generators re-run with no diff. CI's full pytest invocation is running now."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786595877376749001,"uuid":"b4f07e25-a633-4ba1-929a-53b5dce5e48e"}